WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.849 --> 00:00:05.120
It's pretty apparent to most people past puberty
that Disney movies dabble in more than magic

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:05.640
and innocence.

00:00:06.080 --> 00:00:09.760
Take Aladdin, which acts like it's a cute
story of a street savvy kid and a princess

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.420
but which is actually a very weird and uncomfortable
movie when you look a little deeper.

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:17.100
Here are some of the things you only notice
when watching Aladdin as an adult.

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:18.820
Gruesome ends

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:23.480
There are a lot of deaths in Disney films,
but watching as an adult, you start to realize

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:25.420
just how brutal a lot of these movies are.

00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:29.020
For its part, Aladdin kills a lot of people
in some pretty gruesome ways.

00:00:29.380 --> 00:00:33.730
During the song "One Jump Ahead" alone, a
man is impaled on spikes and Abu rips a sword

00:00:33.730 --> 00:00:35.400
out of a guy's throat, likely killing him.

00:00:35.780 --> 00:00:37.240
Then there's this guy from the beginning:

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.520
"A thousand apologies, O patient one."

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:41.980
"You have it then?"

00:00:42.220 --> 00:00:45.360
"I had to slit a few throats, but I got it."

00:00:45.360 --> 00:00:47.920
...who, of course, dies horribly just a few
minutes later.

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:52.520
They're just cartoon characters, sure… unless
you're a four-year-old kid who thinks everything

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:53.140
is alive.

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.540
And then you do this to them?

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.920
"Nooooo!"

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.680
But… but we loved you, Mufasa.

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:05.720
Brothel friends

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.180
During the opening song, Aladdin winds up
in a room with three scantily dressed women,

00:01:10.180 --> 00:01:11.700
all of whom seem pretty familiar with him.

00:01:12.160 --> 00:01:16.120
As an adult, it seems pretty clear that he's
probably in a brothel, and it's a little suspicious

00:01:16.120 --> 00:01:18.460
that the women seem to know Aladdin so well.

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:22.000
It gets even worse, though — when Aladdin
has been prince-ified by the genie and is

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:25.960
arriving at the palace, he shows off for his
lady friends as he travels to meet his future

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:26.480
wife.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:30.200
Kinda makes you see "A Whole New World" in
a very different way.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:31.620
Rat catchers

00:01:32.120 --> 00:01:35.960
At the beginning of the movie, the guards
send dozens of men after one street rat for

00:01:35.960 --> 00:01:37.040
stealing a loaf of bread.

00:01:37.620 --> 00:01:41.149
As a kid, this seems like a fun way to start
off the movie and introduce Aladdin, but as

00:01:41.149 --> 00:01:43.240
an adult, it's pretty obvious overkill.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:44.900
Don't they have better things to do?

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:48.380
There's gotta be worse crimes going on in
Agrabah than a hungry kid stealing food.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:50.800
"All this for a loaf of bread?"

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:52.380
Yeah, no kidding.

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:54.000
Maximum effort

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:58.220
When Jasmine leaves the palace, she gets into
disguise so that the townsfolk won't notice

00:01:58.229 --> 00:02:01.030
who she is — except it's the worst disguise
ever.

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:05.359
Jasmine decides that her "disguise" is going
to be… putting on a hooded robe, and that's

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:07.700
it — leaving her regular outfit and crown
on underneath.

00:02:08.220 --> 00:02:10.840
Even Lois Lane could have figured out that
disguise.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:19.960
She could have at least taken off her crown.

00:02:20.600 --> 00:02:21.700
That's just lazy.

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:23.060
Bad monkey

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:27.180
When you're a kid, Abu seems like a cute sidekick
who provides some much needed humor in the

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:27.920
film's darker moments.

00:02:28.210 --> 00:02:32.100
However, when you're an adult, you pretty
quickly come to realize that Abu is actually

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:32.620
the worst.

00:02:33.220 --> 00:02:36.020
Abu is the one who's reluctant to give his
bread to starving children.

00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:39.780
He's the one who steals a bunch of apples
and jewels even after Jasmine is already this

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:41.300
close to getting her hand cut off.

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:43.740
He's the one who takes that big ruby in the
Cave of Wonders.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:46.000
You know, the one that's obviously a trap.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:50.120
And then, on top of all that, he decides to
cover Aladdin's eyes as they try to fly away.

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:54.500
Yeah, that adorable monkey loses his appeal
for adult viewers pretty quickly.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.120
Supersonic carpet

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:59.940
You gotta love the magic carpet, but how fast
can that thing really fly?

00:03:00.220 --> 00:03:04.500
In "A Whole New World," the magic carpet takes
Aladdin and Jasmine everywhere from Egypt

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:09.280
to Greece to Mulan, all in one night, traveling
slow enough that they can still sing a love

00:03:09.280 --> 00:03:11.220
song without getting the breath sucked out
of their lungs.

00:03:11.560 --> 00:03:14.900
But to reach all those places, the carpet
would have had to fly ridiculously fast.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:16.700
So instead of this...

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:21.140
"But when I'm way up here, it's crystal clear."

00:03:21.820 --> 00:03:23.640
...they would have looked more like this:

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:26.720
And we get it!

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:28.020
It's magic in a kid's movie.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:29.980
But there have to be some ground rules.

00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:31.600
Even the Genie has rules.

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:33.140
Well...sort of.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:34.900
Genie inconsistency

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:38.320
When it comes to wishes, the movie can't seem
to figure out what the Genie can and can't

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:38.840
do.

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:42.560
Aladdin tricks the Genie into getting him
out of the cave without making a wish.

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:43.360
"Hah.

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:44.440
You did that on your own."

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:46.800
"Ugh!

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:49.020
Well, I feel sheepish.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:53.380
But when Jafar's men throw Aladdin off the
cliff and he's literally drowning to death,

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.720
the Genie's suddenly a stickler for the rules:

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:57.120
"Oh, you can't cheat on this one.

00:03:57.120 --> 00:03:58.900
I can't help you unless you make a wish!"

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:01.820
Which… lasts about two seconds until he
saves Aladdin anyway.

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:03.340
What's going on, Genie?

00:04:03.820 --> 00:04:04.860
Jafar is a creep

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:09.980
Okay, so you probably noticed this as a kid,
but it's even more apparent as an adult just

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:11.700
how creepy Jafar is as the film's villain.

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:15.600
He shows basically no interest in Jasmine
throughout the film other than marrying her

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:19.780
so he can take over the throne, and then once
he takes over the kingdom, he basically makes

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:23.100
Jasmine into his sex slave, all to embarrass
her and her father.

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:23.720
Even worse?

00:04:24.120 --> 00:04:26.560
Jasmine is supposedly only 15 years old in
the movie.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:30.940
Jafar is meant to be a villain, but watching
all this as an adult just makes you realize

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:32.560
how disturbing he really is.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.540
It's almost hard to believe that the Sultan
trusts him so much...

00:04:36.080 --> 00:04:40.400
"One thing I pride myself on, Jafar, I'm an
excellent judge of character!"

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.580
"Oh, excellent judge, yeah, sure...

00:04:42.580 --> 00:04:43.200
NOT!"

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:44.860
Thanks for watching!

00:04:44.870 --> 00:04:46.760
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:46.760 --> 00:04:49.220
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

